From 1cca1d7ce6dfcd83a0c0cf7f92c9859ab37e57df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:45:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] fix(outbox): write events inside the caller's
 transaction

Outbox.put committed on its own, so an event could never be part of the
business transaction it describes: a put in the middle of a unit of
work committed everything written so far, and a business write failing
after the put left an orphaned event behind (improvement plan 5.4).

put now only inserts the row and refuses to run outside an open
transaction, so a stray call cannot leave an uncommitted event for some
later commit to pick up. Callers commit or roll back the event together
with their own writes, e.g. inside Database.transaction().

The contract test that documented the auto-commit gap now asserts the
rollback, and the rollback test uses put itself instead of an
equivalent hand-written INSERT.
